# >>> EDGECONNEX GOVERNANCE (managed by EdgeConneX/governance — do not edit) >>>
# Cloud Services is a required approver for two things, and nothing else:
#
#   1. Files that decide WHO OWNS WHAT (CODEOWNERS, in all three locations
#      GitHub will read it from).
#   2. CI/CD -- everything that executes in Actions or reaches a secret. This
#      covers the per-repo pipelines that were built for this repo, not just
#      the shared workflows the governance seeder rolls out. They are protected
#      by default precisely because they are unique to the repo and there is no
#      central copy to restore from.
#
# TEAMS CAN STILL ADD THEIR OWN WORKFLOWS. Anything named team-* is carved out
# below and needs no Cloud Services review -- add, edit and delete freely:
#
#     .github/workflows/team-<whatever>.yml     your own workflow
#     .github/actions/team-<whatever>/          your own composite action
#     .github/scripts/team-<whatever>           scripts your workflow calls
#
# What you cannot do is modify an EXISTING pipeline that is not named team-*.
# That is the point: new work is yours, established CI/CD is reviewed.
#
# WHY A PREFIX AND NOT A governance/ SUBFOLDER: GitHub Actions does not run
# workflows nested in subdirectories of .github/workflows. Verified against the
# live API -- .github/workflows/governance/nested.yml is never registered and
# never runs. A prefix is the only grouping that Actions honours.
#
# Everything else under .github/ is NOT claimed and belongs to the repo's own
# owners: ISSUE_TEMPLATE/, PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md, SECURITY.md,
# CONTRIBUTING.md, FUNDING.yml, labeler and release-note config.
#
# Enforced by the org ruleset "CODEOWNERS protection (governance paths)"
# (required_approving_review_count: 0 + require_code_owner_review: true), whose
# only bypass actors are Cloud Services and the seeder App. Team leads can
# bypass the everyday one-approval rule on repos they own; not this.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so this block is appended last
# and the carve-out is last within it. NOTHING may follow the end marker except
# blank lines and comments -- an ownerless line after it would silently unprotect
# these paths. governance-guard.yml fails the PR if anything else appears there.
#
# Do not edit between these markers — the governance seeder overwrites them.

# --- Who owns what -----------------------------------------------------------
/CODEOWNERS                       @EdgeConneX/cloud-services
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @EdgeConneX/cloud-services
/docs/CODEOWNERS                  @EdgeConneX/cloud-services

# --- CI/CD, protected by default ----------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/               @EdgeConneX/cloud-services
/.github/actions/                 @EdgeConneX/cloud-services
/.github/scripts/                 @EdgeConneX/cloud-services
/.github/dependabot.yml           @EdgeConneX/cloud-services

# --- Team-owned carve-out: NO OWNER, so no review required --------------------
# Must stay last. Adding any other ownerless pattern here, or after the end
# marker, punches a hole in everything above.
/.github/workflows/team-*
/.github/actions/team-*/
/.github/scripts/team-*
# <<< EDGECONNEX GOVERNANCE (managed by EdgeConneX/governance — do not edit) <<<
